  "headline": "Kandy & Knuckles: The Sacred Tooth Temple & a UNESCO Cloud Forest",
  "description": "Kandy was the last capital of the Sinhalese kings and still guards the island’s most sacred relic in the Temple of the Tooth. Drums and conch shells announce the evening puja, and every July or August the Esala Perahera fills the streets with torch-bearers and caparisoned elephants.\n\nAn hour north, the Knuckles range rises into cloud forest — a UNESCO-listed wilderness of ridge trails, remote villages and endemic orchids that I explore with a local botanist.",
